$0(){return this.a.r7(this.b,u.k,"Sova is an accessibility-focused project built during DeerHacks V, designed to help visually impaired users navigate indoor spaces independently. The system combines computer vision, QR\u2011code\u2013based localization, and natural\u2011sounding voice guidance to create a simple but powerful navigation experience.\n\nWhat Sova Does:\n\u2022 Uses a built\u2011in camera on a pair of smart glasses to detect strategically placed QR codes throughout a building.\n\u2022 Scans each code to determine the user\u2019s current location and next steps.\n\u2022 Generates clear, natural voice instructions using the ElevenLabs API, guiding the user from point A to point B without needing braille signs or human assistance.\n\nHow It Works:\n\u2022 QR\u2011based indoor navigation: Each QR code corresponds to a specific location or direction within the building.\n\u2022 Real\u2011time detection: The camera identifies and reads the QR code, which indicates the current and desired location.\n\u2022 AI\u2011generated audio: ElevenLabs converts navigation instructions into high\u2011quality speech delivered directly to the user.\n\u2022 Web app + hardware integration: Built with React, Firebase, and a custom hardware prototype.\n\nTech Stack:\n\u2022 Frontend: React\n\u2022 Backend / Hosting: Firebase\n\u2022 AI Voice: ElevenLabs\n\u2022 Computer Vision: QR code detection via camera feed\n\u2022 Hardware: Logitech Camera acting as a prototype for the glasses\n\nSova was developed in 36 hours and won 3rd place at DeerHacks V.","https://github.com/FurqanAhmad17/sova","assets/sova_thumbnail.png",A.b(["Python","React","Firebase","ElevenLabs","Computer Vision","Accessibility","Hackathon"],t.s))},
